# Snakemake scripts (`scripts/`)

## Bootstrap
- Prefer shared helpers from `scripts/_helpers.py` (`configure_logging`, `set_scenario_config`, `mock_snakemake`).
- Don't invent a new snakemake entry pattern per script; keep wildcards explicit for `mock_snakemake`.

## Config / wildcards
- Wildcard → config updates go through `update_config_from_wildcards()` — don't fork parallel parsers.
- Use `_helpers.get()` for investment-year keyed dicts; don't copy its fallback logic.

## I/O & downloads
- Prefer one download utility (reuse or fix `progress_retrieve`) instead of ad-hoc `requests.get` + tqdm.
- Always set timeouts on HTTP; don't write error HTML bodies to data paths on 403/404.

## Logging
- Use the module logger configured by `configure_logging` — not `print()` for errors/warnings.

## Validation schemas
- Config schema lives under `scripts/lib/validation/`. Runtime helpers belong in `_helpers` or a new `scripts/lib/*.py` — don't grow unrelated logic inside validation modules.

## Tests
- Unit tests for helpers: `test/` + `pixi run unit-tests`.
- Import style: prefer `from scripts.X import ...` consistently (avoid `sys.path.append("./scripts")` in new tests).
